<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qara Khitai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qara Khitai, or Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, was a Central Asian state founded in the twelfth century by Khitan refugees from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after the fall of the Liao dynasty. It defeated the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar">Ahmad Sanjar</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a> in 1141, destroying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. Its lands later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qara-khitai.jpg" alt="Qara Khitai" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Liao.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
